{"SEASON_AUTUMN","",{"Leaves turning, sugar maples are lovely out by Fort Knox","Used to be fall meant the smell of curing tobacco","Autumn... hell, I don't even know what to get ready for","Woodsmoke in the air, somebody's got a stove going","Frost's coming, I feel it in the mornings","Acorns everywhere, squirrels are fat this year","The air smells like apples and wet leaves","Days getting shorter, I count them","Bourbon barrels age better in cool weather, at least somebody's happy","Geese going south - smart birds","Fall, leaves turning, air getting crisp","Golden leaves, red leaves, orange leaves, falling everywhere","Cool nights, warm days, the best of both","Smoke from chimneys, if anyone had chimneys going","Harvest time, if anyone had a harvest"}},
{"SEASON_AUTUMN","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|tmp=seasoned",{"Friday night football was a thing once, whole county showed up","Harvest, whatever's in the fields, take it before the frost"}},
